        },
        "quote": "(1) Restriction of Vehicles to Graded Areas. Construction equipment shall be limited to the actual area to be graded according to the approved grading and erosion control plans. Every effort shall be made to restrict the passage of vehicles over areas intended to be left in their natural state according to approved plans.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.210:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 17.05.210 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "c041cb66-65e7-5d62-bd93-bcc0ab2cba0f",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1086,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.210:block:3",
          "start": 806
        },
        "quote": "(2) Tree Buffer Zone. No grading or operation of heavy equipment shall take place within the areas bounded by the dripline of any tree that is intended to be retained on the site unless an alternate method of preservation of the tree is approved by the Department of Public Works.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.210:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 17.05.210 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "e29ea162-db30-5946-a02c-63f5b14413c4",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1239,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.210:block:4",
          "start": 1087
        },
        "quote": "(3) Protective Barriers. During grading operations the permittee shall provide appropriate barriers around all native vegetation proposed for retention.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.210:block:4#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
